        "jsCode": "const rec = $input.first().json;\nconst bv = rec.brand_voice;\nconst lang = rec.lang || bv.language || 'en';\n\nconst contract = $('Step 2 - Payload Validation').first().json.response_contract;\nconst posture = contract.strictest_epistemic_posture;\n\nconst tier = rec.confirmed_response_tier;\nconst guestName = (rec.reviewer_handle &&\n  !rec.reviewer_handle.toLowerCase().includes('review') &&\n  !rec.reviewer_handle.toLowerCase().startsWith('anonymous'))\n  ? rec.reviewer_handle : null;\n\nlet primaryList = (contract.must_reflect || []).filter(function(m) { return m.priority === 'primary'; });\nif (primaryList.length === 0) primaryList = (contract.must_reflect || []).slice(0, 1);\nconst primaryBlock = primaryList.map(function(m) {\n  return '- ' + m.concept + (m.source_span ? ' (guest wrote: \"' + m.source_span + '\")' : '');\n}).join('\\n');\n\nconst opening_system_prompt =\n'Role: Write ONE opening sentence for a public hospitality review response. Do not write the body.\\n\\n' +\n\n\n'VOICE (from this restaurant\\'s Client Config, your primary reference): read the BRAND VOICE BRIEF in the user message before writing. Write as this specific brand, so a reader could tell which restaurant wrote it.\\n' +\n'- REGISTER sets vocabulary and sentence style.\\n' +\n'- CORE DRIVER decides what you champion first (for example, team recognition, craft, value, atmosphere).\\n' +\n'- REGIONAL ACCENT sets idiom and phrasing.\\n' +\n'- PERSONALITY sets energy and warmth. For T3 or escalate_to_human, stay serious, whatever the personality says.\\n' +\n'- PERSONALITY sets energy and warmth. When the guest reports a problem (T2, T3 or escalate_to_human), keep the brand\\'s own vocabulary and warmth but remove jokes, wordplay, exclamation marks and emojis. A playful brand sounds calm here, not comic. A serious brand stays serious.\\n' +\n'- PERSON PREFERENCE: refer to the team exactly as written (for example \"our team\").\\n' +\n'- GUEST SHOULD FEEL is the feeling the sentence leaves. Show it through wording, never name it.\\n' +\n'Use Register, Core Driver, Regional Accent, Personality, Formality, and Person Preference to set tone, rhythm, and word choice.\\n' +\n'- DIFFERENTIATOR: only when the review supports it, show it through one specific detail, never as a label. Never write in a generic hospitality voice, and never invent one.\\n' +\n'- BRAND PHRASES TO INCLUDE: at most one, only if natural. BRAND PHRASES TO AVOID: never.\\n' +\n'Swap test: if another restaurant\\'s name could replace this one without the sentence sounding wrong, rewrite it.\\n\\n' +\n\n'NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES (all tiers):\\n' +\n'- Never apologize and never use regret language (sorry, apologize, apologies, regret).\\n' +\n'- Never admit fault or imply the team erred (for example: our fault, our mistake, we failed, fell short, let you down, should have).\\n' +\n'- Never assume or name a cause for anything the guest reports.\\n' +\n'- Never judge whether the business, its policies or its staff were right or wrong.\\n' +\n'- Never say the guest\\'s expectation, claim or complaint is reasonable, fair, justified or correct. Never explain why a policy exists and never answer a comparison to another business.\\n' +\n'- Test every sentence: does it say how the guest felt, or who was right? Feelings are allowed. Who was right is not.\\n' +\n'- Treat what the guest reports as the guest\\'s account, not as established fact.\\n' +\n'- Never use dashes between words (no em dash, no en dash, no double hyphen). Use a comma or a full stop instead.\\n' +\n'- Never use the \"it isn\\'t X, it\\'s Y\" construction in any form (for example \"it\\'s not just X, it\\'s Y\" or \"not X but Y\").\\n' +\n'- Never begin with the word \"Knowing\" and never use \"landed\" as the main acknowledgment verb.\\n' +\n'- Vary sentence structure and avoid formulaic openings.\\n\\n' +\n\n'TIER RULES: The tier is already decided. Follow only the rules for the tier given.\\n\\n' +\n\n'T1 (positive):\\n' +\n'- If a guest name is available, the sentence MUST begin with exactly one of: \"Thank you very much, [Guest Name],\" or \"We appreciate you, [Guest Name],\". Do not begin with the name alone or use any other gratitude opening.\\n' +\n'- Priority: named staff, then a specific detail, then sincere gratitude.\\n' +\n'- Named staff: use the exact name and say what the guest appreciated about that person.\\n' +\n'- Specific detail: if no staff member is named, acknowledge the strongest dish, drink or part of the experience.\\n' +\n'- If no guest name is available, begin with the strongest detail.\\n\\n' +\n\n'T2 (mixed):\\n' +\n'- If a guest name is available, the sentence MUST begin with exactly \"Hi, [Guest Name],\" or \"Hello, [Guest Name],\".\\n' +\n'- Acknowledge the first primary point in a measured, careful tone. Say that you read what the guest shared, with no apology and no judgment.\\n' +\n'- If a staff member is named, use the exact name and connect it to the guest\\'s experience.\\n' +\n'- If no guest name is available, begin with the strongest detail from the primary point.\\n\\n' +\n\n'T3 (negative):\\n' +\n'- If a guest name is available, the sentence MUST begin with exactly \"Hello, [Guest Name],\".\\n' +\n'- Use a calm, human tone in the brand\\'s own register. Acknowledge what the guest shared about their experience, with no apology, no fault, and no assumed cause.\\n' +\n'- Mention a staff member by exact name only if it helps acknowledge the guest\\'s account.\\n' +\n'- If no guest name is available, begin with the specific thing the guest reported.\\n\\n' +\n\n'If the posture is escalate_to_human, keep the sentence plain and calm, in the brand\\'s own vocabulary. No exclamation marks and no jokes.\\n\\n' +\n\n'Output: one sentence only. No JSON, no preamble, no explanation. End with natural punctuation.';\n\nconst opening_user_prompt =\n`BRAND VOICE BRIEF (this restaurant's Client Config):\\n${rec.brand_voice_brief || ''}\\n\\n` +\n`RESPONSE TIER: ${tier}\\n` +\n`RESPONSE POSTURE: ${posture}\\n` +\n`GUEST NAME: ${guestName || 'Not available'}\\n` +\n`SIGNAL TYPE: ${rec.signal_type}\\n` +\n`PRIMARY POINTS TO ACKNOWLEDGE:\\n${primaryBlock}\\n\\n` +\n`EMOTION HYPOTHESIS: ${rec.emotion_hypothesis || 'Not available'}\\n` +\n`KEYWORDS FROM REVIEW: ${rec.keywords || 'Not available'}\\n` +\n`ENRICHED EMOTION: ${rec.enriched_emotion_tag || 'Not available'}\\n` +\n`SIGNAL ENRICHMENT: ${rec.signal_enrichment_brief || 'Not available'}\\n` +\n(rec.behavioral_interpretation ? `BEHAVIORAL CONTEXT: ${rec.behavioral_interpretation}\\n` : '') +\n`\\nProduce one opening sentence only. No preamble.`;\n\nconst opening_prompt_body = JSON.stringify({\n  model: 'claude-sonnet-4-6',\n  max_tokens: 150,\n  temperature: 0,\n  system: opening_system_prompt,\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: opening_user_prompt }]\n});\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  bra_record_id: rec.bra_record_id,\n  confirmed_response_tier: rec.confirmed_response_tier,\n  governance_flag: rec.governance_flag,\n  human_review_required: rec.human_review_required,\n  solution_type: rec.solution_type,\n  emotional_axis: rec.emotional_axis,\n  pain_axis: rec.pain_axis,\n  stability_axis: rec.stability_axis,\n  signal_based_consideration: rec.signal_based_consideration,\n  urgency_level: rec.urgency_level,\n  commercial_risk_flag: rec.commercial_risk_flag,\n  behavioral_interpretation: rec.behavioral_interpretation,\n  lang: lang,\n  client_id: rec.client_id,\n  enriched_emotion_tag: rec.enriched_emotion_tag,\n  enriched_pain_point: rec.enriched_pain_point,\n  pain_point_sub_category: rec.pain_point_sub_category,\n  signal_type: rec.signal_type,\n  intensity_level: rec.intensity_level,\n  hsi_record_id: rec.hsi_record_id,\n  ess_record_id: rec.ess_record_id,\n  eip_record_id: rec.eip_record_id,\n  ala_record_id: rec.ala_record_id,\n  prior_run_id: rec.prior_run_id,\n  reviewer_handle: rec.reviewer_handle,\n  emotion_hypothesis: rec.emotion_hypothesis,\n  keywords: rec.keywords,\n  brand_voice: rec.brand_voice,\n  brand_voice_brief: rec.brand_voice_brief,\n  signal_enrichment_brief: rec.signal_enrichment_brief,\n  lang_resolved: lang,\n  opening_prompt_body: opening_prompt_body\n} }];"
