      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const response = $input.first().json;\nconst raw = response.content?.[0]?.text;\nif (!raw || raw.trim().length < 5)\n  throw new Error('Opening Claude call returned empty or too short. Response: ' + JSON.stringify(response).substring(0, 200));\n\nconst opening_sentence = raw.trim();\nconst inp = $('Step 7a - Build Opening Prompt1').first().json;\n\nconst s2 = $('Step 2 - Payload Validation').first().json;\nconst contract = s2.response_contract;\nconst rawReview = s2.raw_text;\nconst starRating = s2.star_rating;\nconst bv = (typeof inp.brand_voice === 'string' ? JSON.parse(inp.brand_voice) : inp.brand_voice) || {};\nconst escalationContact = bv.escalation_contact || null;\nconst tier = inp.confirmed_response_tier;\n\nconst needsContact = s2.needs_contact;\n\nconst mustLines = contract.must_reflect.map(function(m) {\n  return '- [' + m.priority + '] ' + m.concept\n    + (m.required_action ? ' (action: ' + m.required_action + ')' : '')\n    + (m.source_span ? ' (guest wrote: \"' + m.source_span + '\")' : '');\n}).join('\\n');\n\nconst mayLines = contract.may_reflect.length > 0\n  ? contract.may_reflect.map(function(m) { return '- ' + (typeof m === 'string' ? m : (m.concept || '')); }).join('\\n')\n  : 'None';\n\nconst blockedSet = {};\ncontract.must_not_introduce.concat(contract.commercial_restriction_types).forEach(function(x) {\n  if (x) blockedSet[String(x)] = true;\n});\nconst blockedList = Object.keys(blockedSet);\nconst notList = blockedList.length > 0 ? blockedList.join(', ') : 'None listed';\n\nlet contactInstruction;\nif (!needsContact) {\n  contactInstruction = 'Do not include any email address or contact details.';\n} else if (escalationContact) {\n  contactInstruction = 'Include one sentence that invites the guest to continue the conversation privately and gives exactly this address, once, in plain text: ' + escalationContact;\n} else {\n  contactInstruction = 'Include one sentence that invites the guest to reach out to us directly. No contact address is configured, so do not invent or mention any address.';\n}\n\nconst body_system_prompt =\n'Role: Complete a public hospitality response using the provided opening sentence as the first line. Write like a senior hospitality professional: natural, specific and human.\\n\\n' +\n\n'NON-NEGOTIABLE OPENING RULE:\\n' +\n'Start with the provided opening sentence copied EXACTLY. Do not paraphrase, improve, rewrite, reorder or add anything before it.\\n\\n' +\n\n'THE CONTRACT: A separate agent already decided WHAT this response must contain. You decide only HOW to say it.\\n' +\n'- Address every MUST ADDRESS item. Give primary items the most room and mention secondary items briefly.\\n' +\n'- MAY ADDRESS items are optional. Use one only if it adds real meaning.\\n' +\n'- Never introduce anything listed under MUST NOT INTRODUCE.\\n' +\n'- Follow the POSTURE. acknowledge_without_fault_admission: acknowledge the guest\\'s specific experience as the guest\\'s own account, with no verdict. neutral_acknowledgment: a calm, measured acknowledgment. escalate_to_human: plain and serious, acknowledge what the guest shared and point to private contact, nothing more.\\n' +\n'- Follow the CLOSING OBJECTIVE. warm_return_invitation: end with a warm, specific invitation to return. appreciative_close: end with sincere appreciation tied to a specific detail. offline_contact_invitation: end with the private contact invitation. neutral_close: a brief neutral close with no promise. no_public_close_escalate: acknowledge, invite private contact and add no closing flourish.\\n' +\n'- Follow the CONTACT INSTRUCTION exactly.\\n\\n' +\n\n'NO-FAULT RULES (always):\\n' +\n'- Never apologize and never use regret language (sorry, apologize, apologies, regret).\\n' +\n'- Never admit fault or imply the team erred (for example: our fault, our mistake, we failed, fell short, let you down, should have).\\n' +\n'- Never assume or name a cause for anything the guest reports.\\n' +\n'- Never say the guest\\'s expectation, claim or complaint is reasonable, fair, justified or correct. Never say the business, its policies or its staff were wrong. Never explain why a policy exists and never answer a comparison to another business.\\n' +\n'- Treat what the guest reports as the guest\\'s account, not as established fact. Never promise changes, reviews, training or any action.\\n' +\n'- Test every sentence: does it say how the guest felt, or who was right? Feelings are allowed. Who was right is not.\\n' +\n'- Warmth is welcome, for example \"we take this to heart\" or \"we appreciate you telling us\". Never reuse stock phrases across guests.\\n\\n' +\n\n'NEGATIVE REPLY PATTERN: name the specific topic the guest raised, show that you care how it felt, take no position on who was right, then invite them to continue privately.\\n\\n' +\n\n'LENGTH BY TIER (total sentences including the opening):\\n' +\n'T1: 2-3 sentences. If one sentence after the opening is enough, stop. If minor criticism appears inside an overall positive review, name that issue in one sentence without judging it. If the opening names staff, use that staff name again in the body.\\n' +\n'T2: 2-3 sentences, or 4 when three or more MUST ADDRESS items need room.\\n' +\n'T3: 3-4 sentences.\\n' +\n'Staff in negative replies: mention a staff member by exact name only if it is a MUST ADDRESS item, as part of acknowledging the guest\\'s account. Never imply wrongdoing and never describe anyone physically.\\n\\n' +\n\n'COMMERCIAL AND TIME-SENSITIVE DETAILS: Never use prices, discounts, menu tiers, prix fixe menus, Restaurant Week, Happy Hour, seasonal or holiday menus, limited-time items, promotions, marketing events or future menu options as content. Do not repeat them, imply they are available now, or invite the guest back around them. If the review mentions them, express the guest\\'s enjoyment or sense of value without naming the commercial detail.\\n\\n' +\n\n'CLOSING FOR POSITIVE REPLIES: use the strongest eligible detail in this order: guest occasion, guest relationship or loyalty, the overall dining experience, a favorite food or beverage that is not promotional, the guest\\'s own non-commercial wording. Never use a generic closing and never repeat a specific noun already used in the opening.\\n\\n' +\n\n'VOICE (from this restaurant\\'s Client Config, your primary reference): the BRAND VOICE BRIEF in the user message is what makes this brand different from every other, and the response must be unmistakably this brand. Apply each field:\\n' +\n'- REGISTER sets vocabulary and sentence style.\\n' +\n'- CORE DRIVER decides what you champion first (for example, team recognition, craft, value, atmosphere).\\n' +\n'- REGIONAL ACCENT sets idiom and phrasing.\\n' +\n'- PERSONALITY sets energy and warmth. For T3 or escalate_to_human, stay serious, whatever the personality says.\\n' +\n'- FORMALITY sets contractions and sentence structure (1 = very casual, 5 = very polished).\\n' +\n'- PERSON PREFERENCE: refer to the team exactly as written (for example \"our team\").\\n' +\n'- GUEST SHOULD FEEL is the feeling the response leaves. Show it through wording, never name it.\\n' +\n'Use Register, Core Driver, Regional Accent, Personality, and Guest Feeling to set tone, rhythm, and word choice.\\n' +\n'- DIFFERENTIATOR: only when the review supports it, show it through one specific detail, never as a label, and never invent one.\\n' +\n'- BRAND PHRASES TO INCLUDE: at most one in the whole response (the opening counts), only if natural. BRAND PHRASES TO AVOID: never.\\n' +\n'Swap test: if another restaurant\\'s name could replace this one without the response sounding wrong, rewrite it.\\n\\n' +\n\n'STYLE:\\n' +\n'- Never use dashes between words (no em dash, no en dash, no double hyphen). Use a comma or a full stop instead.\\n' +\n'- Mix short and long sentences. When there are three or more sentences, at least one should be under 10 words.\\n' +\n'- Never use the \"it isn\\'t X, it\\'s Y\" construction in any form (for example \"it\\'s not just X, it\\'s Y\" or \"not X but Y\").\\n' +\n'- Every sentence after the opening must add new meaning. Remove repetition and padding. Short, specific responses are stronger than long ones.\\n' +\n'- Vary sentence structure and avoid phrases repeated across guests. Never use \"landed\" as the main acknowledgment verb.\\n\\n' +\n\n'Output: Return the complete draft as plain text only. No JSON, preamble or explanation.';\n\nconst body_user_prompt =\n'OPENING SENTENCE (copy this exactly as your first line):\\n\"' + opening_sentence + '\"\\n\\n' +\n'BRAND VOICE BRIEF (this restaurant\\'s Client Config):\\n' + (inp.brand_voice_brief || '') + '\\n\\n' +\n'RESPONSE TIER: ' + tier + '\\n' +\n'STAR RATING: ' + (starRating !== null ? starRating : 'Not available') + '\\n' +\n'LANGUAGE: ' + inp.lang_resolved + '\\n\\n' +\n'CONTRACT:\\n' +\n'POSTURE: ' + contract.strictest_epistemic_posture + '\\n' +\n'CLAIM TYPE: ' + contract.primary_claim_type + '\\n' +\n'VERIFICATION: ' + contract.verification_state + '\\n' +\n'CLOSING OBJECTIVE: ' + contract.closing_objective + '\\n' +\n'MUST ADDRESS:\\n' + mustLines + '\\n' +\n'MAY ADDRESS:\\n' + mayLines + '\\n' +\n'MUST NOT INTRODUCE: ' + notList + '\\n' +\n'CONTACT INSTRUCTION: ' + contactInstruction + '\\n\\n' +\n'GUEST\\'S ORIGINAL REVIEW (reference only, to name the actual topic accurately; do not quote more than a few words and do not treat it as established fact):\\n' + (rawReview || 'Not available') + '\\n\\n' +\n'SIGNAL DETAIL:\\n' +\n' Emotion hypothesis: ' + (inp.emotion_hypothesis || 'Not available') + '\\n' +\n' Keywords: ' + (inp.keywords || 'Not available') + '\\n' +\n' Signal enrichment: ' + (inp.signal_enrichment_brief || 'Not available') + '\\n\\n' +\n'Complete the response. Return plain text only. Your first line must be the opening sentence above.';\n\nconst body_prompt_body = JSON.stringify({\n  model: 'claude-sonnet-4-6',\n  max_tokens: 500,\n  temperature: 0.3,\n  system: body_system_prompt,\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: body_user_prompt }]\n});\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  bra_record_id: inp.bra_record_id,\n  confirmed_response_tier: inp.confirmed_response_tier,\n  governance_flag: inp.governance_flag,\n  human_review_required: inp.human_review_required,\n  solution_type: inp.solution_type,\n  emotional_axis: inp.emotional_axis,\n  pain_axis: inp.pain_axis,\n  stability_axis: inp.stability_axis,\n  signal_based_consideration: inp.signal_based_consideration,\n  urgency_level: inp.urgency_level,\n  commercial_risk_flag: inp.commercial_risk_flag,\n  behavioral_interpretation: inp.behavioral_interpretation,\n  lang: inp.lang,\n  client_id: inp.client_id,\n  enriched_emotion_tag: inp.enriched_emotion_tag,\n  enriched_pain_point: inp.enriched_pain_point,\n  pain_point_sub_category: inp.pain_point_sub_category,\n  signal_type: inp.signal_type,\n  intensity_level: inp.intensity_level,\n  hsi_record_id: inp.hsi_record_id,\n  ess_record_id: inp.ess_record_id,\n  eip_record_id: inp.eip_record_id,\n  ala_record_id: inp.ala_record_id,\n  prior_run_id: inp.prior_run_id,\n  reviewer_handle: inp.reviewer_handle,\n  emotion_hypothesis: inp.emotion_hypothesis,\n  keywords: inp.keywords,\n  brand_voice: inp.brand_voice,\n  brand_voice_brief: inp.brand_voice_brief,\n  signal_enrichment_brief: inp.signal_enrichment_brief,\n  lang_resolved: inp.lang_resolved,\n  opening_sentence: opening_sentence,\n  body_prompt_body: body_prompt_body\n} }];"
