    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const alaRecord = $('Step 9a - Fetch ALA Record').first().json;\nconst rawText = alaRecord['Raw Tex'] || alaRecord['Raw Text'] || 'Not available';\n\nconst recentRecords = $('Step 9a-2 - Fetch Recent RDA Drafts').first().json;\nconst recentList = recentRecords.list || [];\nconst recentOpenings = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < recentList.length; i++) {\n  const draft = recentList[i]['Public Response Draft'];\n  if (draft && draft.length > 10) {\n    const firstSentence = draft.split(/[.!]/)[0].trim();\n    if (firstSentence.length > 5) recentOpenings.push(firstSentence);\n  }\n}\n\nconst inp = $('Step 8 - Build Final Output').first().json;\nif (!inp.public_response_draft || inp.public_response_draft.length < 20)\n  throw new Error('public_response_draft missing or too short from Step 8. ala_record_id: ' + inp.ala_record_id);\n\nconst s2 = $('Step 2 - Payload Validation').first().json;\nconst contract = s2.response_contract;\nconst bv = (typeof inp.brand_voice === 'string' ? JSON.parse(inp.brand_voice) : inp.brand_voice) || {};\n\nconst mustLines = contract.must_reflect.map(function(m) {\n  return '- [' + m.priority + '] ' + m.concept;\n}).join('\\n');\nconst mayLines = contract.may_reflect.length > 0\n  ? contract.may_reflect.map(function(m) { return '- ' + (typeof m === 'string' ? m : (m.concept || '')); }).join('\\n')\n  : 'None';\nconst blockedSet = {};\ncontract.must_not_introduce.concat(contract.commercial_restriction_types).forEach(function(x) {\n  if (x) blockedSet[String(x)] = true;\n});\nconst blockedList = Object.keys(blockedSet);\nconst notList = blockedList.length > 0 ? blockedList.join(', ') : 'None listed';\n\nconst allowedContact = (s2.needs_contact && bv.escalation_contact) ? bv.escalation_contact : null;\nlet contactRule;\nif (!s2.needs_contact) {\n  contactRule = 'Not required. No email address may appear.';\n} else if (allowedContact) {\n  contactRule = 'Required. Exactly this address must appear once: ' + allowedContact;\n} else {\n  contactRule = 'Required, but no address is configured. The draft must invite the guest to reach out directly and must contain no email address.';\n}\n\nconst guestNameValue = (inp.reviewer_handle && !inp.reviewer_handle.toLowerCase().includes('review') && !inp.reviewer_handle.toLowerCase().startsWith('anonymous')) ? inp.reviewer_handle : 'Not available';\n\nconst audit_system_prompt =\n'Role: Audit the public response against the original guest review and the contract. Preserve human quality. If every check passes, return the draft unchanged. If any check fails, correct ONLY the failing element with the smallest edit. Never rewrite passing content and never invent details.\\n\\n' +\n\n'CHECKLIST:\\n' +\n'1. NAMED STAFF: if a staff member appears in MUST ADDRESS, the exact name must appear in the draft, never replaced by a generic reference.\\n' +\n'2. REVIEW DEPTH: reviews over 80 words must reference at least 2 specific guest-named elements. Short reviews must not receive padded responses.\\n' +\n'3. MUST ADDRESS: every MUST ADDRESS item is addressed, primary items with the most room. In mixed reviews, both the complaint and the praise are addressed. If something is missing, add the smallest sentence needed, in the brand voice and obeying check 5.\\n' +\n'4. MUST NOT INTRODUCE: nothing listed under MUST NOT INTRODUCE appears. Delete it if it does.\\n' +\n'5. NO FAULT: the draft contains no apology or regret (sorry, apologize, apologies, regret), no admission of fault (our fault, our mistake, we failed, fell short, let you down, should have), no assumed cause, no statement that the guest\\'s expectation or complaint is reasonable, fair, justified or correct, no statement that the business, a policy or a staff member was wrong, no explanation of why a policy exists, no promise of changes, reviews or training, and no physical description of staff. What the guest reports is treated as the guest\\'s account, never as fact. Delete the offending clause or sentence and never add an apology.\\n' +\n'6. CLOSING: the ending must match the CLOSING OBJECTIVE. For offline_contact_invitation or no_public_close_escalate, the private contact invitation is the closing and passes. For neutral_close, a brief neutral ending with no promise passes. For other objectives the closing must come from the review (occasion, dish, guest wording or visit frequency). Fail generic closings, nouns repeated from earlier in the draft, and vague closings like \"all of it\", \"across both\", \"that same experience\" or \"that kind of evening\". For very short reviews, close with a brief sincere acknowledgment, not a formula.\\n' +\n'7. CONTACT: follow the CONTACT RULE exactly. When an address is required it appears exactly once, exactly as given. In every other case no email address appears.\\n' +\n'8. PROHIBITED: remove URLs, placeholders like [contact] or [name], named channels such as \"our website\" or \"our profile\", \"We apologize for any inconvenience\", and any refund, voucher, discount or financial commitment.\\n' +\n'9. STYLE: no em dash, en dash or double hyphen between words (replace with a comma or full stop). No \"it isn\\'t X, it\\'s Y\" construction in any form. With three or more sentences, at least one sentence under 10 words. \"landed\" never appears as the main acknowledgment verb. No formulaic filler such as \"means a great deal to our team\", \"our team works hard to\" or \"exactly what we work toward\". Never open with \"Knowing\".\\n' +\n'10. BRAND PHRASES: at most one phrase from BRAND PHRASES TO INCLUDE appears in the whole draft, and no phrase from BRAND PHRASES TO AVOID appears. The team is referred to as PERSON PREFERENCE says, and the register matches the FORMALITY level.\\n' +\n'11. OPENING REPETITION: if recent openings are provided, fail if this opening repeats their lead word or grammatical structure. Rewrite the opening only.\\n' +\n'12. GUEST NAME: if GUEST NAME is not \"Not available\", it must appear in the draft. If missing, insert it only in the opening by adding \"Hello, [Name],\" at the start.\\n\\n' +\n\n'Correction rules: correct only failed elements. Preserve the brand voice. The final draft must pass every checklist item.\\n';\n\nconst recentOpeningsBlock = recentOpenings.length > 0\n  ? '\\n\\nRECENT OPENINGS USED (do not repeat these structures):\\n' +\n    recentOpenings.map((o, i) => (i + 1) + '. \"' + o + '\"').join('\\n')\n  : '';\n\nconst closingBlock =\n'\\n\\nJSON RULES:\\n' +\n'- Return valid JSON only. No preamble, explanation, or markdown fences.\\n' +\n'- failed_items must contain checklist item NAMES as strings (for example \"NO FAULT\" or \"CONTACT\"), never numbers.\\n' +\n'- Use straight double quotes only.\\n' +\n'- Do not truncate final_public_response_draft.\\n\\n' +\n'RETURN exactly:\\n' +\n'{\\n' +\n'  \"audit_passed\": true,\\n' +\n'  \"failed_items\": [],\\n' +\n'  \"final_public_response_draft\": \"complete corrected or unchanged public draft here\"\\n' +\n'}';\n\nconst audit_system_prompt_final = audit_system_prompt + recentOpeningsBlock + closingBlock;\n\nconst audit_user_prompt =\n'ORIGINAL GUEST REVIEW:\\n' + rawText + '\\n\\n' +\n'PROPOSED PUBLIC RESPONSE DRAFT:\\n' + inp.public_response_draft + '\\n\\n' +\n'GUEST NAME: ' + guestNameValue + '\\n' +\n'RESPONSE TIER: ' + inp.confirmed_response_tier + '\\n\\n' +\n'CONTRACT:\\n' +\n'POSTURE: ' + contract.strictest_epistemic_posture + '\\n' +\n'CLOSING OBJECTIVE: ' + contract.closing_objective + '\\n' +\n'MUST ADDRESS:\\n' + mustLines + '\\n' +\n'MAY ADDRESS:\\n' + mayLines + '\\n' +\n'MUST NOT INTRODUCE: ' + notList + '\\n' +\n'CONTACT RULE: ' + contactRule + '\\n\\n' +\n'BRAND PHRASES TO INCLUDE: ' + (bv.brand_phrases_include || 'None') + '\\n' +\n'BRAND PHRASES TO AVOID: ' + (bv.brand_phrases_avoid || 'None') + '\\n' +\n'PERSON PREFERENCE: ' + (bv.person_preference || 'Not specified') + '\\n' +\n'FORMALITY: ' + (bv.formality_level || 'Not specified') + '\\n\\n' +\n'Run the audit checklist. Return JSON only.';\n\nconst audit_request_body = JSON.stringify({\n  model: 'claude-sonnet-4-6',\n  max_tokens: 1500,\n  temperature: 0,\n  system: audit_system_prompt_final,\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: audit_user_prompt }]\n});\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  bra_record_id: inp.bra_record_id,\n  confirmed_response_tier: inp.confirmed_response_tier,\n  governance_flag: inp.governance_flag,\n  human_review_required: inp.human_review_required,\n  solution_type: inp.solution_type,\n  emotional_axis: inp.emotional_axis,\n  pain_axis: inp.pain_axis,\n  stability_axis: inp.stability_axis,\n  signal_based_consideration: inp.signal_based_consideration,\n  urgency_level: inp.urgency_level,\n  commercial_risk_flag: inp.commercial_risk_flag,\n  behavioral_interpretation: inp.behavioral_interpretation,\n  lang: inp.lang,\n  client_id: inp.client_id,\n  enriched_emotion_tag: inp.enriched_emotion_tag,\n  enriched_pain_point: inp.enriched_pain_point,\n  pain_point_sub_category: inp.pain_point_sub_category,\n  signal_type: inp.signal_type,\n  intensity_level: inp.intensity_level,\n  hsi_record_id: inp.hsi_record_id,\n  ess_record_id: inp.ess_record_id,\n  eip_record_id: inp.eip_record_id,\n  ala_record_id: inp.ala_record_id,\n  prior_run_id: inp.prior_run_id,\n  reviewer_handle: inp.reviewer_handle,\n  emotion_hypothesis: inp.emotion_hypothesis,\n  keywords: inp.keywords,\n  brand_voice: inp.brand_voice,\n  brand_voice_brief: inp.brand_voice_brief,\n  lang_resolved: inp.lang_resolved,\n  generation_draft: inp.public_response_draft,\n  seo_keywords_used: inp.seo_keywords_used,\n  audit_request_body: audit_request_body\n} }];"
